      "file": "app/views/patients/_filters.html.erb",
      "note": "False positive. The href is always a trusted path helper plus an escaped query string: `url` is a local the two callers pass as patients_path (index.html.erb:26) or potentials_patients_path (potentials.html.erb:24) \u2014 never user input \u2014 and the rest is request.query_parameters run through to_query, which percent-encodes. So the value cannot begin with javascript: or any other scheme. Brakeman flags it because it cannot see where the `url` local comes from. Reviewed 2026-10-05."
    },
    {
      "fingerprint": "3ec659183d85c6b81161fc9ab02fc16594c5d94889d231456ff44d7080fcbfcd",
      "file": "app/models/patient.rb",
      "note": "False positive. Every value interpolated into the CASE comes from Patient::STATE_REVIEW_ORDER, a frozen constant: the states go through connection.quote and the ranks are integer literals in that same constant. No request data reaches this string. The Arel.sql wrapper is required because Rails will not accept a raw ordering expression otherwise. Reviewed 2026-10-05."
    },
    {
      "fingerprint": "21ab0fe00fdd5899ffc405cff75aadb91b805ee996a614f7e27b08a287e9062d",
      "file": "Gemfile.lock",
      "note": "REAL, not a false positive \u2014 silenced deliberately so one dated advisory does not hold the whole build red, and tracked as task U1 in CLAUDE.md instead. The Rails 8.0 series stops receiving SECURITY fixes on 2026-11-07 (bug fixes already stopped on 2026-05-07), so the fix is moving to 8.1 \u2014 its own piece of work with its own test run, not something to slip into an unrelated deploy. REMOVE THIS ENTRY as part of that upgrade: leaving it would silence the next EOL warning too, which is the failure mode that makes ignore files dangerous. Noted 2026-10-05. NB the date is Brakeman's own data and it moved between gem versions (8.0.5 said 2026-10-07, 8.1.0 says 2026-11-07); rubyonrails.org/maintenance is the authority, not this file."
    }
